# PRify — Cursor AI Rules

## Project Type
Pure frontend web app (HTML/CSS/JS). No backend, no Node.js, no npm, no build step.

## Tech Stack
- Vanilla HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript (ES Modules)
- SheetJS (xlsx) via CDN for Excel parsing
- Wikipedia REST API for celebrity bios
- Google Gemini API for AI tweet generation
- Hosted on GitHub Pages

## Rules
1. All code is client-side browser JavaScript — never suggest Node.js or server-side code
2. Use ES Modules (import/export) for all JS files
3. Use const by default, let when mutation needed, never var
4. Use async/await for async operations
5. Use JSDoc comments for all exported functions
6. Use textContent (not innerHTML) for user data to prevent XSS
7. SheetJS is loaded via CDN script tag — access via window.XLSX
8. Gemini API key is stored in localStorage only
9. Process celebrities sequentially with delays to avoid rate limiting
10. All error handling should show user-friendly messages in the UI
11. Keep functions small and single-purpose
12. CSS uses custom properties (variables) defined in :root
13. No external CSS frameworks — custom styles only
14. Responsive design using CSS Grid/Flexbox
